es its failures behind professional titles.\n\nWhen regulators block deployment to wait for hypothetical safety certainty, they assign an infinite price to future risk while treating the immediate human toll of disease and wrongful incarceration as free. Every week spent delaying the rollout of diagnostic algorithms and recidivism audits condemns real people to suffer under a failing status quo that human oversight cannot fix. The moral indictment of delay rests on a simple empirical reality: abundance and fairness arrive through rapid iteration, open evaluation, and decentralized experimentation, never through central planning and precautionary paralysis. Who gave anyone the right to freeze innovation and force vulnerable populations to wait indefinitely for a medical cure or a fair trial that cautious bureaucracy will never deliver?",
